Alternative for API-07: format ratios with "%.15g" (always <= ~25 chars, cannot
overflow) after rejecting non-finite values. Rejected as the recommended one:
it changes the saved strategy text ("0.05" instead of "0.050000"), which is
visible through SCOTCH_stratSave and golden-output tests. Shown for part_ovl.

--- a/src/libscotch/library_graph_part_ovl.c
+++ b/src/libscotch/library_graph_part_ovl.c
@@ SCOTCH_stratGraphPartOvlBuild @@
-  sprintf (kbaltab, "%lf", balrat);
+  if ((! isfinite (balrat)) || (balrat < 0.0)) {
+    errorPrint (STRINGIFY (SCOTCH_stratGraphPartOvlBuild) ": invalid imbalance ratio");
+    return (1);
+  }
+  snprintf (kbaltab, sizeof (kbaltab), "%.15g", balrat);
